    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2ab5686d-0c37-5bac-b059-ccc82b87cf88",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $y=\\frac{- 2 e^{x}}{x + 4}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=- 2 e^{x}$ and $v=x + 4.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}&=- 2 e^{x}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}&=\\frac{v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}-u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}}{v^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(x + 4)\\cdot (- 2 e^{x})-(- 2 e^{x})\\cdot (1)}{(x + 4)^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{- 2 e^{x}(x+4-1)}{(x + 4)^{2}}\\\\ &=- \\frac{2 \\left(x + 3\\right) e^{x}}{\\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "49a3ff36-52c0-5b41-828f-a868642253fb",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "aefc96f0-5fbf-5f07-8483-7ac12e8610e9",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "- \\frac{2 \\left(x + 3\\right) e^{x}}{\\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
